with a bit of character.

1033
00:57:12.553 --> 00:57:14.721
Would that be old ones
or new ones?

1034
00:57:15.306 --> 00:57:16.640
Today. an old one.

1035
00:57:16.807 --> 00:57:17.808
[Sharon] Today?

1036
00:57:19.268 --> 00:57:20.727
I need to be
in your line of work.

1037
00:57:20.811 --> 00:57:21.687
[both chuckle]

1038
00:57:22.354 --> 00:57:23.981
So what are we driving today?

1039
00:57:24.148 --> 00:57:26.858
[sighs] If you can guess.
I'll give you the keys to it.

1040
00:57:27.026 --> 00:57:28.027
Ooh.

1041
00:57:28.569 --> 00:57:29.570
Be careful.

1042
00:57:29.736 --> 00:57:30.737
I'm good at this.

1043
00:57:30.904 --> 00:57:31.947
- Yeah?
- Mmm-hmm.

1044
00:57:32.114 --> 00:57:33.115
All right.

1045
00:57:33.282 --> 00:57:35.993
Okay. I'm gonna go with
a Chevy Chevelle.

1046
00:57:36.618 --> 00:57:37.869
Color?

1047
00:57:38.204 --> 00:57:39.455
Racing green.

1048
00:57:40.706 --> 00:57:41.915
Right color.

1049
00:57:43.792 --> 00:57:45.211
Well. one out of two.
that's not bad.

1050
00:57:45.377 --> 00:57:46.503
[Davis] Not bad at all.

1051
00:57:46.670 --> 00:57:48.797
[Sharon] That is
a beautiful car. though.

1052
00:57:50.424 --> 00:57:51.925
I underestimated you.

1053
00:57:52.093 --> 00:57:53.177
Mike.

1054
00:57:53.344 --> 00:57:54.511
Sharon.

1055
00:57:54.678 --> 00:57:55.846
Nice to meet you. Mike.

1056
00:57:56.013 --> 00:57:57.389
[Davis] Nice to meet you. too.

1057
00:58:04.063 --> 00:58:05.064
- [door closes]
- [engine starts]

1058
00:58:08.609 --> 00:58:10.027
[key clacking]

1059
00:58:11.362 --> 00:58:12.779
- [operator] Like I said...
- [Tillman] No...

1060
00:58:12.946 --> 00:58:15.116
[operator] ...that's
the last image we have.

1061
00:58:15.282 --> 00:58:17.368
[Lou] Are you certain
that we don't pick him up

1062
00:58:17.534 --> 00:58:19.245
on the 101
in either direction?

1063
00:58:19.411 --> 00:58:21.122
[operator sighs]
Still certain.

1064
00:58:23.582 --> 00:58:26.335
Somewhere between that turn
and the 101. he switched cars.

1065
00:58:26.502 --> 00:58:27.878
Why are you so convinced
he took the 101?

1066
00:58:28.045 --> 00:58:29.046
Hey. don't ask. man.

1067
00:58:29.213 --> 00:58:31.632
Look. there's 30 blocks
between there and the 101.

1068
00:58:31.798 --> 00:58:33.050
- Let's get lookin'.
- Are you serious?

1069
00:58:33.217 --> 00:58:34.926
- [Lou] I'm serious.
- Lou. come on. man.

1070
00:58:35.094 --> 00:58:36.220
[Lou] How else
are we gonna find him?

1071
00:58:36.887 --> 00:58:38.722
[Maya] The books
come with the place?

1072
00:58:39.140 --> 00:58:40.599
- Uh-huh.
- [Maya] Huh.

1073
00:58:43.269 --> 00:58:44.603
For someone
who likes things...

1074
00:58:44.770 --> 00:58:46.397
you don't
really have a lot of...

1075
00:58:47.564 --> 00:58:48.857
personal stuff.

1076
00:58:51.277 --> 00:58:53.195
No photos of family or...

1077
00:58:56.448 --> 00:58:57.741
Do you have any?

1078
00:58:57.908 --> 00:58:58.992
What? Photos?

1079
00:58:59.160 --> 00:59:01.120
[chuckles] No. Family.

1080
00:59:02.037 --> 00:59:03.038
Yeah. someplace.

1081
00:59:03.664 --> 00:59:04.790
Someplace?

1082
00:59:04.956 --> 00:59:06.292
- What. like in a drawer?
- [Davis chuckles]

1083
00:59:07.000 --> 00:59:08.794
I don't know. we're just
not really that kinda family.

1084
00:59:08.960 --> 00:59:10.254
Don't really keep in touch.

1085
00:59:10.421 --> 00:59:11.463
I don't know.

1086
00:59:11.630 --> 00:59:13.965
Do you have.
like. brothers? Sisters?

1087
00:59:14.133 --> 00:59:16.052
- Mom? Dad?
- [knife clangs]

1088
00:59:17.428 --> 00:59:19.305
Yeah. Yeah.

1089
00:59:19.471 --> 00:59:20.889
I don't know.
we didn't really. uh.

1090
00:59:21.056 --> 00:59:22.224
have a lot of stuff growin' up

1091
00:59:22.391 --> 00:59:23.892
and whatever we did have.

1092
00:59:24.059 --> 00:59:25.352
I didn't really
keep any of it.

1093
00:59:26.895 --> 00:59:27.896
So...

1094
00:59:28.814 --> 00:59:30.816
[mellow music playing]

1095
00:59:39.408 --> 00:59:40.409
What?

1096
00:59:41.202 --> 00:59:42.494
Mystery man.

1097
00:59:47.583 --> 00:59:48.667
Yeah.

1098
00:59:49.376 --> 00:59:51.420
[Maya] Can I turn on
some music?

1099
00:59:52.338 --> 00:59:53.464
[Davis] Yeah.

1100
00:59:53.630 --> 00:59:56.049
There's a thing in the corner.

1101
00:59:58.135 --> 00:59:59.220
Do you have a favorite song?

1102
01:00:01.222 --> 01:00:02.764
Um...

1103
01:00:02.931 --> 01:00:04.600
[Maya] No. Okay.

1104
01:00:04.766 --> 01:00:06.017
I don't know why I would ask

1105
01:00:06.185 --> 01:00:08.604
why you would have
a favorite song.

1106
01:00:08.770 --> 01:00:10.731
[Davis] Suppose that's
another black mark. huh?

1107
01:00:10.897 --> 01:00:11.898
[Maya chuckles]

1108
01:00:12.691 --> 01:00:13.859
[Maya] Aye. yai. yai...

1109
01:00:14.025 --> 01:00:15.652
- Do you. um...
- [device beeps]

1110
01:00:15.819 --> 01:00:17.779
Do you listen to music or...

1111
01:00:18.405 --> 01:00:19.490
Yeah. sometimes.

1112
01:00:19.573 --> 01:00:20.449
[soft rock song playing]

1113
01:00:20.532 --> 01:00:21.783
[Maya] Sometimes?

1114
01:00:22.951 --> 01:00:24.119
You don't. do you?

1115
01:00:29.375 --> 01:00:30.584
Come on.

1116
01:00:32.253 --> 01:00:33.670
I can't dance.

1117
01:00:40.927 --> 01:00:42.012
Come on.

1118
01:00:43.096 --> 01:00:44.515
Come on.

1119
01:00:47.184 --> 01:00:48.185
Come here.

1120
01:00:48.352 --> 01:00:52.105
No photos.
no music. no dancing.

1121
01:00:52.731 --> 01:00:55.817
Someone needs to teach you
how to be a human.

1122
01:00:55.984 --> 01:00:56.985
Yeah.

1123
01:01:00.197 --> 01:01:01.282
[Maya laughs]

1124
01:01:03.992 --> 01:01:05.619
[crowd cheering
over music player]

1125
01:01:05.786 --> 01:01:06.870
Ah.

1126
01:01:07.788 --> 01:01:09.122
I love that.

1127
01:01:10.291 --> 01:01:14.211
They cheer for home.
but no one does that for LA.

1128
01:01:21.343 --> 01:01:22.678
[crowd cheering
over music player]

1129
01:02:12.436 --> 01:02:13.437
[song fades]

1130
01:02:14.646 --> 01:02:15.731
[Maya] Happy?

1131
01:02:19.067 --> 01:02:20.068
Yeah.

1132
01:02:24.406 --> 01:02:25.449
Yeah.

1133
01:02:30.496 --> 01:02:31.497
Scared?

1134
01:02:36.543 --> 01:02:37.628
Yeah. maybe.

1135
01:02:40.213 --> 01:02:41.214
[exhales]

1136
01:02:41.382 --> 01:02:43.384
[mellow music playing]

1137
01:02:58.273 --> 01:02:59.483
You're not gonna stay?

1138
01:03:13.121 --> 01:03:14.122
[exhales softly]

1139
01:03:18.794 --> 01:03:20.211
[Maya] Do you want me to stay?

1140
01:03:21.838 --> 01:03:22.839
[Davis] Yeah.

1141
01:03:29.971 --> 01:03:31.056
Good.

1142
01:03:39.565 --> 01:03:40.566
[door opens]

1143
01:03:45.195 --> 01:03:46.029
[door closes]

1144
01:04:05.173 --> 01:04:07.175
[tense music playing]

1145
01:04:25.694 --> 01:04:27.070
[engine starts]

1146
01:04:39.833 --> 01:04:40.876
[breathing heavily]

1147
01:04:46.339 --> 01:04:47.382
[grunts]

1148
01:04:47.549 --> 01:04:49.510
[panting]

1149
01:04:50.051 --> 01:04:50.886
[Davis grunts]

1150
01:05:01.980 --> 01:05:02.981
[line beeps]

1151
01:05:03.148 --> 01:05:04.941
[Davis] <i>Hi. this is Mr. Stone.</i>

1152
01:05:05.108 --> 01:05:06.067
<i>I need a new apartment</i>

1153
01:05:06.234 --> 01:05:08.612
<i>on the beach
available immediately.</i>

1154
01:05:10.906 --> 01:05:11.740
[door thuds]

1155
01:05:27.297 --> 01:05:29.425
[doorbell buzzing]

1156
01:05:34.680 --> 01:05:35.681
[Devon] Can I help you?

1157
01:05:35.847 --> 01:05:36.848
[Ormon] <i>Got delivery
for Wilson.</i>

1158
01:05:37.015 --> 01:05:38.642
I'm not expecting anything.

1159
01:05:38.809 --> 01:05:39.976
[Ormon] <i>It's got
your name on it.</i>

1160
01:05:40.143 --> 01:05:42.438
All right.
Just leave it outside.

1161
01:05:42.604 --> 01:05:43.480
[Ormon] <i>I'm not allowed
to do that.</i>

1162
01:05:43.647 --> 01:05:44.981
[sighs] All right.
Leave it in the hall.

1163
01:05:45.148 --> 01:05:46.149
[door buzzes]

1164
01:05:52.781 --> 01:05:53.907
- [door thuds]
- [Devon] Whoa!

1165
01:05:54.074 --> 01:05:55.450
[Devon gasping]

1166
01:05:55.617 --> 01:05:58.787
[Ormon] Move.
Come on. move. Move.

1167
01:05:59.580 --> 01:06:01.540
[both grunting]

1168
01:06:04.167 --> 01:06:05.043
Huh?

1169
01:06:07.003 --> 01:06:09.422
You're gonna tell me what you
fucking gave him. okay?

1170
01:06:10.674 --> 01:06:11.800
Fucking tell me.

1171
01:06:11.883 --> 01:06:12.801
[panting]

1172
01:06:14.720 --> 01:06:15.679
[Tillman] How many
more of these

1173
01:06:15.846 --> 01:06:17.556
fucking garages you gonna
make us do tonight. man?

1174
01:06:18.682 --> 01:06:19.975
[Tillman sighs]

1175
01:06:20.141 --> 01:06:21.142
Hey. man...

1176
01:06:24.312 --> 01:06:26.064
- Let's take a look.
- Have you...

1177
01:06:26.231 --> 01:06:28.483
- See there?
- What? Now what?

1178
01:06:39.452 --> 01:06:40.370
Lou.

1179
01:06:40.537 --> 01:06:41.538
[car alarm beeping]

1180
01:06:42.122 --> 01:06:42.956
[sighs deeply]

1181
01:06:43.498 --> 01:06:45.333
Fuck's sake. man.

1182
01:06:56.803 --> 01:06:58.054
[mumbles] Mmm. Huh.

1183
01:07:03.685 --> 01:07:04.686
Call forensics.

1184
01:07:04.853 --> 01:07:06.437
[man] Black
wasn't a color for him.

1185
01:07:06.605 --> 01:07:08.273
It was his whole subject.

1186
01:07:08.439 --> 01:07:09.482
[woman] I wouldn't
put it on my wall

1187
01:07:09.650 --> 01:07:12.068
but I do love
the sense of drama.

1188
01:07:12.235 --> 01:07:14.988
I think you can be confident
it's not gonna lose its value.

1189
01:07:15.155 --> 01:07:16.740
The real question is...

1190
01:07:16.907 --> 01:07:18.199
how much do you love it?

1191
01:07:18.366 --> 01:07:19.576
Well. I love it.

1192
01:07:19.743 --> 01:07:21.536
It'll go great
with the new chairs. you know.

1193
01:07:21.703 --> 01:07:23.371
[Andrew] Really?
You sure you want this guy

1194
01:07:23.538 --> 01:07:25.999
glaring down at us
every time we have dinner?

1195
01:07:26.082 --> 01:07:27.000
[Beth] He's not glaring.

1196
01:07:27.083 --> 01:07:28.084
[Andrew] He's glaring.

1197
01:07:28.251 --> 01:07:30.211
[Beth] I'm sure.
And he isn't glaring. really.

1198
01:07:30.378 --> 01:07:31.212
He's just looking. you know.

1199
01:07:31.296 --> 01:07:32.255
Excuse me.
I'll be right with you.

1200
01:07:32.338 --> 01:07:33.339
- [Beth] Okay.
- Sure. Thank you.

1201
01:07:35.842 --> 01:07:37.678
Well. what a coincidence.

1202
01:07:37.844 --> 01:07:38.845
[Davis] Hey.

1203
01:07:39.012 --> 01:07:40.013
Uh. Sharon. right?

1204
01:07:40.180 --> 01:07:41.181
- [Sharon] Yeah.
- Yeah.

1205
01:07:41.347 --> 01:07:42.766
- Mike?
- That's it.

1206
01:07:42.933 --> 01:07:44.225
- Yeah. good to see you.
- [Sharon] Hmm.

1207
01:07:45.602 --> 01:07:46.436
Uh...

1208
01:07:47.020 --> 01:07:49.522
So do you collect art
like you do cars. Mike?

1209
01:07:49.690 --> 01:07:51.107
Uh. not really. but I like it.

1210
01:07:52.150 --> 01:07:53.902
I like the sense of drama.

1211
01:07:54.444 --> 01:07:56.487
[glass clinking]

1212
01:07:57.113 --> 01:07:57.948
[Sharon] Hmm.

1213
01:08:00.366 --> 01:08:02.202
Hey. do you maybe
wanna get out of here?

1214
01:08:02.368 --> 01:08:04.204
Grab a drink or something?

1215
01:08:05.080 --> 01:08:06.832
[Tillman] I swear. man...

1216
01:08:06.998 --> 01:08:08.291
you divorced guys.
you always think

1217
01:08:08.458 --> 01:08:09.292
you're gonna move to the beach

1218
01:08:09.459 --> 01:08:11.252
and meet
some hot surfer chick.

1219
01:08:11.419 --> 01:08:13.338
What you gonna do?
Take up surfing?

1220
01:08:13.504 --> 01:08:16.257
No. I'm gonna...
Thinking of doing the yoga.

1221
01:08:17.508 --> 01:08:18.719
The yoga?

1222
01:08:20.261 --> 01:08:21.471
[Tillman laughs]

1223
01:08:21.638 --> 01:08:23.807
'Course. you are. What kind?

1224
01:08:24.474 --> 01:08:25.684
They got kinds?

1225
01:08:25.851 --> 01:08:27.102
Big time. man.

1226
01:08:27.268 --> 01:08:30.480
They got hot yoga. fast yoga.

1227
01:08:30.647 --> 01:08:32.565
street yoga. Greek yoga.

1228
01:08:32.733 --> 01:08:34.735
- Greek yoga?
- That last one might be food.

1229
01:08:34.901 --> 01:08:36.319
[Tillman chuckling]

1230
01:08:36.486 --> 01:08:38.196
So. you just wanna get laid.

1231
01:08:38.363 --> 01:08:39.405
Oh. man. I wanna get fit.

1232
01:08:39.572 --> 01:08:40.949
- Fitness?
- [sighs]

1233
01:08:41.116 --> 01:08:43.118
- Please. booze man. you...
- [Lou] What's up?

1234
01:08:43.284 --> 01:08:44.535
It's like a new car.

1235
01:08:44.703 --> 01:08:46.079
Fuck.

1236
01:08:46.246 --> 01:08:48.289
Except for one
microscopic speck of blood.

1237
01:08:49.624 --> 01:08:51.334
[Tillman] Is it enough
to get DNA?

1238
01:08:51.501 --> 01:08:52.753
[forensics officer] Should be.

1239
01:08:52.919 --> 01:08:54.087
Let me see.

1240
01:08:56.047 --> 01:08:57.966
[Davis] So. I guess
you work in the art world?

1241
01:08:58.633 --> 01:09:00.301
[Sharon] Nope. Less glamorous.

1242
01:09:00.468 --> 01:09:02.929
I write insurance policies
for people

1243
01:09:03.096 --> 01:09:05.181
who have more money than
they know what to do with.

1244
01:09:05.974 --> 01:09:06.850
[Davis] So. you must know

1245
01:09:06.933 --> 01:09:08.143
a lot about
what things are worth. huh?

1246
01:09:08.309 --> 01:09:10.520
Mmm-hmm. Too much.

1247
01:09:10.687 --> 01:09:12.022
But I also have to know a lot

1248
01:09:12.188 --> 01:09:14.065
about the people
that own these things.

1249
01:09:14.149 --> 01:09:15.066
How do you mean?

1250
01:09:15.150 --> 01:09:16.651
[Sharon] You know.
are you a thrill seeker.

1251
01:09:17.235 --> 01:09:19.279
are you an alcoholic.
do you gamble.

1252
01:09:19.445 --> 01:09:20.655
do you cheat on your partner?

1253
01:09:20.822 --> 01:09:22.532
You know. all those questions
that you can't ask

1254
01:09:22.699 --> 01:09:25.035
but you obviously need to know
the answers to.

1255
01:09:25.869 --> 01:09:28.496
So. you get real good
at reading people.

1256
01:09:28.955 --> 01:09:31.332
And what have you.
uh. read about me?

1257
01:09:32.167 --> 01:09:33.418
[Sharon chuckles]

1258
01:09:33.584 --> 01:09:34.585
Mmm-mmm.

1259
01:09:35.420 --> 01:09:36.713
Things you don't like or what?

1260
01:09:36.797 --> 01:09:37.714
[Sharon] Mmm-mmm.

1261
01:09:37.798 --> 01:09:39.925
Nope. No. did not say that.

1262
01:09:41.217 --> 01:09:42.052
[Sharon chuckles]

1263
01:09:42.135 --> 01:09:43.303
Come on.

1264
01:09:45.889 --> 01:09:46.890
Okay.

1265
01:09:47.808 --> 01:09:51.102
[sighs] Well. you look like
a person who has secrets.

1266
01:09:51.269 --> 01:09:52.729
- Is that right?
- [Sharon] Mmm-hmm.

1267
01:09:52.896 --> 01:09:54.773
Your shirt's new
or newly pressed

1268
01:09:54.940 --> 01:09:56.900
which says you don't
do your own laundry

1269
01:09:57.067 --> 01:09:58.318
or you're a bit OCD.

1270
01:09:58.484 --> 01:09:59.736
Uh. you're very groomed.

1271
01:10:00.111 --> 01:10:01.612
Your hair. your nails.

1272
01:10:01.780 --> 01:10:03.782
your 12-thousand-dollar
watch there.

1273
01:10:04.449 --> 01:10:06.076
everything is just. uh...

1274
01:10:07.202 --> 01:10:08.578
a little too perfect.

1275
01:10:08.745 --> 01:10:10.246
Which tells me
you have a lot of money

1276
01:10:10.413 --> 01:10:12.332
and a lot of time
on your hands. Mike.

1277
01:10:13.166 --> 01:10:14.500
Got the clothes. the cars...

1278
01:10:14.667 --> 01:10:16.795
but you can't seem
to look me in the eye.

1279
01:10:16.962 --> 01:10:19.881
And I'd bet
you didn't grow up with money.

1280
01:10:21.716 --> 01:10:22.717
How do you figure that?

1281
01:10:23.051 --> 01:10:26.387
Because people who grow up
in chaos crave order.

1282
01:10:29.265 --> 01:10:30.892
You talkin' about me or you?

1283
01:10:32.310 --> 01:10:33.519
Maybe both.

1284
01:10:36.439 --> 01:10:38.024
That hit too close to home?

1285
01:10:40.026 --> 01:10:41.027
No.

1286
01:10:43.947 --> 01:10:45.281
I have a...

1287
01:10:45.949 --> 01:10:47.951
[clears throat]
I have a confession to make.

1288
01:10:48.118 --> 01:10:49.119
